[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-77677"] :question/problem "Consider the line $y=2x-5$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $y=2x-5$ passes through the points $A(0,-5)$ and $B(1,-3)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $A$ and $B$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${A}^{′}(5,0)$ and ${B}^{′}(4,2).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-0 & =\\frac{2-0}{4-5}(x-5) \\\\ y & =-2(x-5) \\\\ y & =-2x+10 \\\\ 2x+y-10 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-77776/selection/8cfba76abc42ac0d6adf03fc6069d51f9f3647a081ae35e945757274838f4b93" :answer/id #uuid "b842027f-3e17-54b4-a2d1-ffe6e2b3cf0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8x+13y+2=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77776/selection/9b5aa6915915e7a0de2c47bb2d20eed376ccf7494be2cd0a51411293faf6e3e3" :answer/id #uuid "73f7fd2a-8954-5b8d-92f4-2fbd1546f8b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13x+8y+2=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77776/selection/29c1d3f662dc987fdf8af9c495becea4235af30b2fe37e8b552b34b961a387d1" :answer/id #uuid "08fd19ea-c633-517a-b1c9-ee6f8212d9fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13x+3y+2=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77776/selection/ce6f5e2542607a3d6afcd5b82033819525c58bec51ff35b7da60a4fe832dde5d" :answer/id #uuid "b8e4427b-7761-5a55-b634-a5cadfd2e927" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8x+3y+2=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77776/selection/5def8e60c5034d441f63c1567f0cdd57be62cf1f411994babe2432600daf0ac9" :answer/id #uuid "613759be-094a-5654-974d-97ea77254189" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8x+3y+12=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77776/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "625f4560-f4c4-52df-8e53-891c0a200f7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-77776/selection/8cfba76abc42ac0d6adf03fc6069d51f9f3647a081ae35e945757274838f4b93" :answer-field/choices ["q-77776/selection/8cfba76abc42ac0d6adf03fc6069d51f9f3647a081ae35e945757274838f4b93" "q-77776/selection/9b5aa6915915e7a0de2c47bb2d20eed376ccf7494be2cd0a51411293faf6e3e3" "q-77776/selection/29c1d3f662dc987fdf8af9c495becea4235af30b2fe37e8b552b34b961a387d1" "q-77776/selection/ce6f5e2542607a3d6afcd5b82033819525c58bec51ff35b7da60a4fe832dde5d" "q-77776/selection/5def8e60c5034d441f63c1567f0cdd57be62cf1f411994babe2432600daf0ac9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-77776" :question/id #uuid "8a72a83e-c00c-5e25-8dc9-1f34b89688c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-77776" :question/problem "Consider the line $y=4x-1$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $y=4x-1$ passes through the points $Q(0,-1)$ and $R(1,3)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $Q$ and $R$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -10 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${Q}^{′}(3,-2)$ and ${R}^{′}(-10,6).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${Q}^{′}$ and ${R}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-2) & =\\frac{6-(-2)}{-10-3}(x-3) \\\\ y+2 & =-\\frac{8}{13}(x-3) \\\\ 13y+26 & =-8x+24 \\\\ 8x+13y+2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-77776/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c8f0fa1-a86a-577f-bdc9-fc7427faa18d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77776"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-77794/selection/103602f6c0f17a056a315f53d7cbd10d4d14180ae680de668ce7901345870144" :answer/id #uuid "69731315-f5ae-5cde-bab7-d1978c4bba63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x-y+5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77794/selection/b5703ed57969338f34927acb8d178311de65f34f34a6af983cb32510b8019557" :answer/id #uuid "2fd26bd2-454c-5a54-bcb1-4e5502c04eb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x+2y-8=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77794/selection/0b18c48579e6c25c5604c81dfc966a75d01015911465cae5c00eb32f4a146d3c" :answer/id #uuid "99ce92ea-9c05-5f30-bc0c-e0abe132458c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+y-2=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77794/selection/603729029ccc8453a41d72a740427fa59ea6e62a89397211946e7902e73dc084" :answer/id #uuid "17e2ac8a-c6f6-5c22-9f7b-9ab72c08574d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+y+5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77794/selection/50a8c1cc761f12060fb6a0a9ce77a91a88b96c8bf6831e02b9bd8883fa742bf9" :answer/id #uuid "b5832623-0d39-5f11-af80-e02249e69fbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x+y-5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77794/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c7424fbf-0429-5b72-9977-1b822a27aee7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-77794/selection/b5703ed57969338f34927acb8d178311de65f34f34a6af983cb32510b8019557" :answer-field/choices ["q-77794/selection/103602f6c0f17a056a315f53d7cbd10d4d14180ae680de668ce7901345870144" "q-77794/selection/b5703ed57969338f34927acb8d178311de65f34f34a6af983cb32510b8019557" "q-77794/selection/0b18c48579e6c25c5604c81dfc966a75d01015911465cae5c00eb32f4a146d3c" "q-77794/selection/603729029ccc8453a41d72a740427fa59ea6e62a89397211946e7902e73dc084" "q-77794/selection/50a8c1cc761f12060fb6a0a9ce77a91a88b96c8bf6831e02b9bd8883fa742bf9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-77794" :question/id #uuid "0a4b4ce2-c004-5f79-8440-fc9bd932b630" :question/math-academy-id "q-77794" :question/problem "Consider the line $x=1$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $x=1$ passes through the points $J(1,0)$ and $K(1,1)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $J$ and $K$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${J}^{′}(2,1)$ and ${K}^{′}(0,4).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${J}^{′}$ and ${K}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =\\frac{4-1}{0-2}(x-2) \\\\ y-1 & =-\\frac{3}{2}(x-2) \\\\ 2y-2 & =-3x+6 \\\\ 3x+2y-8 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-77794/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15e8730b-c59a-5897-8c83-073b54f517a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77794"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-278618/field-1/5bf277e0ab740a6123bc5ebf4cd75428f233e831942b13f057c16e2c9867c114" :answer/id #uuid "b90b6209-8665-5bca-a65f-38f2dcde1a08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7x+6y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278618/field-1/85992148a2e96acce4094cfb0302c37ebbb65b2cd3028af6fca36a8b77139155" :answer/id #uuid "2bfa5bbc-041c-50c4-a6ab-8e28ee16640c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6x+7y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278618/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d8fb79a2-9b20-52bc-b059-160737f01f4a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278618/field-1/5bf277e0ab740a6123bc5ebf4cd75428f233e831942b13f057c16e2c9867c114" :answer-field/choices ["q-278618/field-1/5bf277e0ab740a6123bc5ebf4cd75428f233e831942b13f057c16e2c9867c114" "q-278618/field-1/85992148a2e96acce4094cfb0302c37ebbb65b2cd3028af6fca36a8b77139155"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278618" :question/id #uuid "525cff54-b46c-5657-adcf-4b43e73bacde" :question/math-academy-id "q-278618" :question/problem "Consider the line $y=3x+5$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=-40.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $y=3x+5$ passes through the points $A(0,5)$ and $B(1,8)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $A$ and $B$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 & -16 \\\\ 5 & 12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${A}^{′}(-10,5)$ and ${B}^{′}(-16,12).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-5 & =\\frac{12-5}{-16-(-10)}(x-(-10)) \\\\ y-5 & =-\\frac{7}{6}(x+10)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-5 & =-\\frac{7}{6}(x+10) \\\\ 6y-30 & =-7x-70 \\\\ 7x+6y & =-40\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-278618/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c8f0fa1-a86a-577f-bdc9-fc7427faa18d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278618"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-281578/field-1/d59853570c5b460ce82039da4c45edbb24defb7000d6534b07ba956d55440103" :answer/id #uuid "9424cfe2-6854-51f6-9245-1820857efc9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281578/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f65cea3e-96ef-5463-a59e-68d962ad2ab7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-281578/field-1/d59853570c5b460ce82039da4c45edbb24defb7000d6534b07ba956d55440103" :answer-field/choices ["q-281578/field-1/d59853570c5b460ce82039da4c45edbb24defb7000d6534b07ba956d55440103"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-281578" :question/id #uuid "835dea08-d02f-5695-b6e8-88ac1d402393" :question/math-academy-id "q-281578" :question/problem "Consider the line $x=4$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=16.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $x=4$ passes through the points $G(4,0)$ and $H(4,1)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $G$ and $H$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 & 10 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${G}^{′}(12,4)$ and ${H}^{′}(10,6).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${G}^{′}$ and ${H}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-4 & =\\frac{6-4}{10-12}(x-12) \\\\ y-4 & =-1(x-12)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-4 & =-x+12 \\\\ x+y & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-281578/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15e8730b-c59a-5897-8c83-073b54f517a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-281578"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
